## Why this answer is the only answer

<!-- For a forward task, uniqueness is about the QUESTION, not the system —
     the system is fully specified, so the solution exists and is unique.
     What has to be argued is that the quantity you asked for is unambiguous:
     over what interval, at what point, in what frame, with what convention.

     Write out the definition precisely, then read problem.md back and check it
     forces that definition and no other. Ambiguity here is the single most
     common reason a forward task fails QA — two competent people compute two
     different, defensible numbers. -->

